Changelog: 17-10-2026 13:24:38

Release 0.2.1.

Changelog: 17-10-2026 12:58:02

Fixed. The app's folder in the suite is apps/ppsspp (was apps/ppsspp-manager) and its package is ppsspp_manager
(was bc250_ppsspp_manager): the suite's naming convention (owner, 17-10-2026), a short folder name and the package
named after the app without the BC-250 prefix; both names are the owner's. With the folder go its key in the
portal, its chapter of the wiki (apps/ppsspp/, which the Manual link opens), its installer test and its release
tags: ppsspp-v<x.y.z> from the next release on, which the app's update check follows. The installed app keeps its
name, its launcher bc250-ppsspp-manager, the run wrapper bc250-ppsspp-run that the Steam shortcuts start, its folder
under ~/.local/share with the installed PPSSPP, and its settings; the portal moves its record of the installed copy
to the new key.

